2. Lab source code: MIT
   Applies to: the source code, scripts and Makefiles inside labs/*.zip (starter programs, test programs,
   demo programs, shell scripts), and the JavaScript inside present/*.html and labs/*.html (the slide viewer
   and the browser tools), except the files listed in 3 and 4 below. A lab file shown inside labs/labNN.html
   keeps the licence it has in the zip.
   You may use, copy, modify and redistribute this code, including in your own projects, under the
   MIT License: LICENSES/MIT.txt (text reproduced below).

3. Linux kernel modules: GPL-2.0
   Applies to: every source file inside labs/lab14_files.zip and labs/lab15_files.zip that starts with
   "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0" (the kernel modules and their starters). Kernel modules that use the
   kernel's GPL-only interfaces must be GPL-licensed.
   License: GNU General Public License, version 2 only: LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt

4. Third-party files (not written by the author; their own licences apply)
   - labs/lab14_files.zip and labs/lab15_files.zip: guest/busybox, a static BusyBox 1.36.1 binary from
     Ubuntu 24.04 (package busybox-static, version 1:1.36.1-6ubuntu3.1). License: GPL-2.0-only.
     Corresponding source: https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/busybox (Ubuntu) and https://busybox.net (upstream).
   - labs/lab09_files.zip: tables/syscall_32.tbl, tables/syscall_64.tbl, tables/asm-generic_unistd.h,
     copied from the Linux kernel source (v6.8). License: GPL-2.0 (the header: GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note,
     as stated in its SPDX line). Source: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git
   - labs/lab09.html embeds the same syscall_64.tbl, and the errno names, numbers and comments from the
     Linux UAPI headers asm-generic/errno-base.h and asm-generic/errno.h (GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note).
   - assets/fonts/: IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono, Copyright IBM Corp. License: SIL Open Font License 1.1
     (assets/fonts/OFL.txt).
   - Short excerpts of Linux kernel source code quoted on the slides (with file names and line numbers,
     Linux v6.8) remain under the kernel's licence, GPL-2.0.
   - Book titles and section numbers are cited for reference only; no book content is reproduced.

No warranty: the materials are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Run kernel code only in a
virtual machine, as the labs instruct.

